```sh
uv run pytest                                            # unit tests, with an 80% coverage floor
[% if has_cli %]
uv run pytest tests/unit/test_config.py -k env --no-cov  # a subset, no coverage floor
[% else %]
uv run pytest tests/unit/test_version.py --no-cov        # a subset, no coverage floor
[% endif %]
RUN_INTEGRATION=1 uv run pytest -m integration --no-cov  # integration tests (real external systems), no coverage floor
```

CI runs the unit tests on every supported Python version, together with ruff, mypy (strict), the wiki checks and the manifest checks. All of them block a merge.
[% if integration_ci %]

The **Integration tests** job runs the integration tests too, with every package in `contrib/system-packages.txt`[% if integration_extras %] and the extras the Copier answer `integration_extras` names[% endif %]. It fails if no test runs or one is skipped, so a missing package or device fails it rather than passing it.
[% endif %]
